    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f374df033bc1dd11dbb5004063a8fdfab6b95911be5a7c13f111fceb3de38a3a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Separated arcs and Wronskian nondegeneracy make the local derivative/second-derivative coordinate map invertible, which converts the high-dimensional multilinear curve expression into a product of planar quadratic expressions. Planar decoupling then drives a scale bootstrap, and in the four-dimensional A6 geometry periodic enlargement and a second local expansion repeat this planar reduction at finer frequency scales.",
